  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">State Owned Enterprises Reform Activity (SOERA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aimed at supporting the Government of Ukraine (GOU) and other stakeholders enhance public sector governance and property management, including planning and advancing critical reforms of Ukraine&#x2019;s State-Owned Enterprises (SOEs)), improving GOU management of state and municipal assets, sustaining a wartime economy and ensuring a swift and transparent reconstruction at the war&#x2019;s end.
The project will focus on 5 main components:
1.	SOE Mapping, Information, and Strategy
2.	 Establishing Reform Coordinating Mechanism and Strategic Communications
3.	Reviewing and Improving Public Asset Management Policies, Legislation, and regulations
4.	Facilitating SOE Utilization and Privatization
5.	Improving Corporate Governance, Management, and Performance of SOEs
6.	Providing Emergency Response and Recovery Preparation Technical Assistance to the GOU and SOEs</narrative>
  </description>
